# Resigning writes the SGF result on the root and adds no move node, so it can
# only ever describe the end of the line being played. Applied while reviewing,
# it used to relabel the whole record: rewind a game White resigned, press
# Resign as Black, and the result flipped to "black resigned" while the recorded
# moves still ended the other way. The saved SGF contradicted itself.
#
# The toolbar greyed the Resign button in that state, but the keybinding did
# not, so the corruption was reachable anyway. GobanControl::canResign() is now
# the single predicate behind both.

new_game 9
wait_idle
switch_player black human
switch_player white human
wait_idle

# Black passes, then White resigns: RE[B+R], reported as white_resigned.
pass
wait_until move_count >= 1
wait_idle
resign
# The phase flips in endGame(), which runs before the record is written, so wait
# on the thing being asserted rather than on the phase.
wait_until result white_resigned
wait_idle
expect phase finished
expect move_count 1

# Rewind into the game. The phase leaves Finished; the record keeps its result.
navigate_back
wait_idle
expect phase paused
expect view_position 0
expect result white_resigned

# Resigning here must be refused — there is a continuation ahead of the cursor.
# Before the fix this rewrote the root to "black resigned".
resign
# Phase first: the guard refuses before the command's model.start(), so a
# regression shows up here immediately. `result` lags — the move would be
# handed to the game thread — so it is the corroborating check, not the canary.
expect phase paused
wait_idle
expect phase paused
expect result white_resigned
expect move_count 0

# And it is still refused after returning to the end, because the game there is
# already decided; resigning twice would overwrite the recorded outcome.
navigate_end
wait_idle
expect phase finished
resign
wait_idle
expect result white_resigned
